ped with the help of Stanford Professor of Psychology, Michael Frank Ph.D. •Personalized daily activity plan with fun-filled activities tailored to your baby’s needs – not the “average” child. Your plan will be set-up to teach the right skills at the right time, taking into account your baby’s sensitive developmental periods. Kinedu works on four growth areas – including cognitive, linguistic, physical, as well as social and emotional development. The activities recommended are based on the child's development by fun short videos that model each activity and teach your child through play. Download Kinedu today and discover fun and age-appropriate developmental activities to entertain and encourage your baby's development! Subscription details: Kinedu can be downloaded for FREE. Our free version allows you to use our app and to create a profile for your baby, personalize his or her plan with our milestone assessment, access to a few sample activities, milestone checklist, and other developmental information. If you choose to become a premium member, you will unlock 1,000+ early developmental activities, the catalog section, access to detailed progress reports, add family members or your nanny, and add up to 5 babies to your account. You can become a Premium member through: - You can subscribe to Kinedu as a premium member through a monthly (1-month), auto-renewing in-app subscription. You can also subscribe to Kinedu through a yearly (1-year) auto-renewing in-app subscription, or a Lifetime subscription (one-time payment). - The Monthly subscription is priced at $9.99 USD or it's equivalent in local currency. -The Yearly subscription is priced at $89.99 USD or it's equivalent in local currency -The Lifetime subscription is priced at $149.99 USD or it's equivalent in local currency -Subscription automatically renews unless auto-renew is turned off at least 24-hours before the end of the current period. - Your account will be charged for renewal within 24-hours prior to the end of the current period, and identify the cost of the renewal -Subscriptions may be managed by the user and auto-renewal may be turned off by going to the user's Account Settings after purchase. You can view our privacy policy and terms of use at http://blog.kinedu.com/privacy-policy/\n\n## Ratings & Reviews\n\n  * 4.3\n\nout of 5\n\n4 Ratings\n\n## What’s New\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPlaying Preschool: Homeschool Preschool Program - Busy Toddler (https://shop.busytoddler.com/product/playing-preschool-complete-program/)\nciteturn89search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month; \n\nBusy Toddler\n\nmaking it to naps, one activity at a time\n\nSale!\n\n# Playing Preschool Year 1\n\n~~$39.90~~ $29.90\n\nPreschool is so much more than memorizing the ABCs and 123s. Playing Preschool Year 1 is a comprehensive, secular, play-based program designed to build a strong educational foundation while honoring how young children learn best. Across 19 thoughtfully sequenced units, children build skills in literacy, math, science, art, and motor development through carefully selected read-alouds, curated discussions, and hands-on activities.\n\nChildren investigate ideas, make connections, and share their thinking as they grow their understanding of the world around them. Skills build in complexity throughout the year, giving children the time and experience they need to develop as curious and confident learners. Playing Preschool combines thoughtful lesson plans with detailed guidance to make preschool at home doable, joyful, and effective.\n\nPages: 314 pages of lesson plans and resources\nProgram Length: 38 weeks of fully planned lessons\nDaily Time: Approximately 45-60 minutes per lesson\nRecommended Ages: 2.5 to 5 years old\nSubjects: Early literacy, mathematics, science, sensory exploration, fine arts, and motor development\n\nAuthored by Susie Allison, M. Ed.\n\nThis program is sold as a non-refundable digital PDF.\n\nCategory: ebook\n\n  * Description\n\n## More About Playing Preschool Year 1\n\nPlaying Preschool Year 1 is a 314-page PDF. You will receive immediate access and an email with a link to your online profile with lifetime access to your purchase.\n\nPlaying Preschool was carefully designed to support parents because the early years should be joyful, not stressful. In addition to the daily lesson plans, you will also receive:\n\n  * A Start-Up Guide to help you teach with confidence from the very first lesson\n  * A full book list for each of the 19 thematic units\n  * Detailed supply lists for every unit\n  * More than 350 hands-on activities\n  * Nineteen unit poems and songs to build phonemic awareness\n\nThis program is sold as a non-refundable digital PDF.\n\n## Discover the Magic of Playing Preschool\n\nYou are your child’s best teacher, and with the Playing Preschool program, you’ll have everything you need to make that happen.\n\nImage: ABC blocks iconImage: ABC blocks icon\n\n### Play-Based\n\nMeaningful learning through play, not worksheets or drills. Every activity is designed to teach through hands-on discovery, not pages to fill out.\n\nImage: magnifying glass iconImage: magnifying glass icon\n\n### Intentional\n\nEvery lesson is designed for you and your child to do together, turning ordinary days into lifelong memories you’ll both treasure.\n\nImage: crayons iconImage: crayons icon\n\n### Low-Prep\n\nMaterials and instructions are laid out for you, lesson by lesson. Open the program, gather from the unit supply lists, and start teaching.\n\nImage: calendar iconImage: calendar icon\n\n### Structured\n\nA clear, planned rhythm for every single day. You’ll always know what’s next, without having to build it yourself or fill in blanks.\n\nImage: puzzle iconImage: puzzle icon\n\n### Open-Ended\n\nPlaying Preschool meets your child where they are, with room to grow and explore at their own pace. The program flexes and adapts to the child.\n\nImage: Ho